cff-version: 1.2.0
title: AI-Enabled Drug Discovery and Synthesis - Colab notebooks
message: If you use these notebooks in research or teaching, please cite them.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Sunil
    family-names: Paliwal
    affiliation: Department of Chemistry and Chemical Biology, Stevens Institute of Technology
    # orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0000-0000-0000"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Sunil-Paliwal/ai-enabled-drug-discovery-and-synthesis"
abstract: >-
  Four Colab notebooks for computer-aided molecular design: molecular
  interactions, structural validity and alerts, bioisosteric replacement, and
  retrosynthesis. Usable for research as well as teaching -- the structural
  validation module includes a batch mode that reports validity rate and the
  breakdown of failure modes across a set of generated structures. Each module
  also ships a worksheet that asks the user to predict before running and to
  judge what the tool cannot tell them.
keywords:
  - cheminformatics
  - drug design
  - chemistry education
  - generative model evaluation
  - RDKit
  - structural alerts
  - bioisostere
